    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0141" n="651" xml:id="pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/2–2348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d56-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-23T23:00:00-05:00">February 23,
                            1948—11 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Inform Austin and Rusk immediately. Latter at Hotel Vanderbilt. Following
                    message received from President Truman: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Your draft statement which it is proposed Senator Austin make before
                            Security Council Tuesday 24 February is approved. In regard to public
                            statement by me I intend to release the following: <quote
                                rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘The Palestina-problem has been, and is the deep concern of this
                                    Government. It has been given the most careful consideration by
                                    me, the Cabinet, and other responsible Government officials. The
                                    US position has been developed through long and exhaustive study
                                    and many consultations.</p>
                                <p>This position has been accurately presented by Ambassador Austin
                                    in his speech before the Security Council of the United Nations
                                    today.’</p>
                            </quote>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please notify me as soon as Senator Austin has made his presentation to the
                    Security Council.”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d56-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d56-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d56-f1-content">
                <p>The President’s top secret and urgent message was transmitted to Secretary
                    Marshall in telegram Blue 8, at 7:29 p. m. EST
                    February 23 (copy in Elsey Papers).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d56-f2" n="2" xml:id="d56-f2-content">
                <p>President Truman released his public statement later on February 24, while still
                    aboard the <hi rendition="#italic">Williamsburg</hi>. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents of the United States:
                        Harry S. Truman, 1948</hi>, p. 39.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
